00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:10.080
so

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:11.840
i just did what i consider to be one of

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:15.280
the most difficult things to do

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:20.160
in my profession of acting which is

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:20.160
to walk as yourself

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.880
this is the first time in my life i have

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:28.800
ever actually talked about my work

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:31.199
in this way i didn't go to drama school

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:32.399
the first time in fact i remember seeing

00:00:31.199 --> 00:00:34.559
drama at all

00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:35.440
was when my mother took me to an amateur

00:00:34.559 --> 00:00:38.480
production of

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.760
ham it was a cataclysmic experience a

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:41.840
darkened space

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.200
with a group of people watching

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:46.399
something and they're

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:46.399
transformed by it

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.920
i would like to share some of the ways i

00:00:49.039 --> 00:00:52.079
work

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:54.079
never act in front of a mirror you are

00:00:52.079 --> 00:00:57.280
doing the exact opposite

00:00:54.079 --> 00:00:59.280
of what acting is about acting is all

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:01.280
about what's happening within you

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:02.559
it doesn't matter what's happening on

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:05.199
your face

00:01:02.559 --> 00:01:07.600
it's a collaboration between us all your

00:01:05.199 --> 00:01:10.159
costume designer is incredibly important

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:11.439
in building your character a russian

00:01:10.159 --> 00:01:14.479
with a bad wig

00:01:11.439 --> 00:01:16.080
and these glasses nomination likewise

00:01:14.479 --> 00:01:17.360
the environment is going to tell the

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:20.720
story of the character

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:20.720
as much as the costume is

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:24.799
i knew nothing at all about working in

00:01:23.439 --> 00:01:27.520
front of a camera

00:01:24.799 --> 00:01:28.240
now this is what happens just before you

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.479
do a take

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:32.079
at this point you have to cut all this

00:01:30.479 --> 00:01:33.920
stuff out

00:01:32.079 --> 00:01:35.840
and when the director calls action you

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:38.320
don't have to start acting straight away

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:39.280
of course the beautiful moment is

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:43.680
between you

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:43.680
and that little spot next to the lens

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:48.640
i remember this feeling so well and many

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:52.479
of you will feel it

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:55.360
when suddenly you're in control of it

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:56.320
i felt i was on this incredibly powerful

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:58.479
horse

00:01:56.320 --> 00:02:00.079
but i had the vocal ability i had the

00:01:58.479 --> 00:02:02.719
intellectual ability

00:02:00.079 --> 00:02:04.000
for that all to settle and now i could

00:02:02.719 --> 00:02:06.240
play with it

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.200
the moment where your technique is so

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:09.119
deep within you

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:11.280
that gives you the freedom then to

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:15.200
invent to improvise

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:23.840
to act i'm helen mirren

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:23.840
and this is my master class

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.280
you

